[expr.type.conv]/2 + [dcl.init.list]/3.10: a braced-init-list with
no elements for a scalar type performs value-initialization
(yielding zero).  CBMC currently rejects T{} at type-check time for
primitive T with "cannot initialize 'signed int' with an initializer
list" and produces a CONVERSION ERROR.

Discovered while writing a positive test for [temp.point] that used
T{} as a generic zero producer.
